## Who This Documentation Is For

- **Project contributors**: contributors maintaining this repository,
	adding modules, ETL processes, and rules, and updating
	template-generated files.

	See the [Contributing](contributing/) section of this documentation
	for information on how to change workflow code, update generated
	template layers, and keep tests and docs in sync.

	See the [Overview](overview/) section of this documentation to
	understand the project structure, design principles, and key parts
	of the generated workflow.

- **Project users**: people who run the workflow from this repository
	against their own data.

	See the [Setup](setup/) and [Workflow](workflow/) sections of this
	documentation for information on installing the project, configuring
	local runs, and using `config/config.local.yaml` for machine-specific
	overrides.

- **Project integrators**: people who import this workflow as a
	Snakemake module or import Python package components such as
	`schema` and `extract` into an outer project.

	See the [Workflow](workflow/) section of this documentation for
	configuration and execution details, and review the relevant module,
	dataset, feature, or model pages for the interfaces exposed by this
	project.

